From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bdx-iot-external <noreply@bdx-iot-external>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] imx8mp-debix-model-a: add dummy mcu_rdc node for SPL

SPL's board_handle_rdc_config() (arch/arm/mach-imx/spl.c) unconditionally
looks up an "imx8m,mcu_rdc" node to configure the Cortex-M7 RDC before/after
release, even though this board doesn't use the M7 core. Without the node
SPL prints two harmless but noisy "Failed to find node!, err: -1!" errors
on every boot. Add a no-op node (single all-zero terminator entry) so the
lookup succeeds and the RDC configuration applied is a no-op.

Signed-off-by: bdx-iot-external <noreply@bdx-iot-external>
---
 arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-debix-model-a-u-boot.dtsi | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-debix-model-a-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-debix-model-a-u-boot.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-debix-model-a-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-debix-model-a-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -8,6 +8,12 @@
 #include "imx8mp-u-boot.dtsi"
 
 / {
+	mcu_rdc {
+		compatible = "imx8m,mcu_rdc";
+		start-config = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
+		stop-config = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
+		bootph-pre-ram;
+	};
 	wdt-reboot {
 		compatible = "wdt-reboot";
 		wdt = <&wdog1>;
--
2.34.1
